From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:20:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sdc: read_sdc tracks an empty command with a flag, not a
 compare
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

include_file reads a file a line at a time, appending each line to the
command until it is complete, and asked `$cmd == ""` on every line to
know whether a command was starting. A command that spans many lines,
as write_sdc writes an exception over every register (one line per
object), made that comparison read the growing command once per line.

Read at Tcl's global scope, Tcl did not keep the command's character
count between lines and every comparison walked the whole command:
XiangShan's MemBlock synthesis .sdc (1.65 million lines, six exceptions
over 268,694 registers each) took over 15 minutes in read_sdc, against
53 s with this change. Read from inside a proc, as ORFS does, it took
56 s before and after. A flag says whether the command is empty; the
constraints read are the same.

Not upstreamed. Carried in bazel-orfs; retires on the //:bump onto an
OpenROAD whose OpenSTA has it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 tcl/Util.tcl | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/openroad/sta/tcl/Util.tcl b/openroad/sta/tcl/Util.tcl
index e3d09a2d..b14f53e5 100644
--- a/openroad/sta/tcl/Util.tcl
+++ b/openroad/sta/tcl/Util.tcl
@@ -630,6 +630,9 @@ proc include_file { filename echo verbose } {
         zlib push gunzip $stream
       }
       set cmd ""
+      # Whether cmd holds no lines yet: comparing cmd with "" would read the
+      # whole of a command spanning many lines once per line.
+      set cmd_empty 1
       set error {}
       set error_traceback {}
       while {![eof $stream]} {
@@ -639,7 +642,8 @@ proc include_file { filename echo verbose } {
             report_line $line
           }
         }
-        if { $cmd == "" } {
+        if { $cmd_empty } {
+          set cmd_empty 0
           set cmd_start_line $include_line
           set check_complete 1
         }
@@ -653,6 +657,7 @@ proc include_file { filename echo verbose } {
           set error_code [catch {uplevel \#0 $cmd} result error_options]
           # cmd consumed
           set cmd ""
+          set cmd_empty 1
           # Flush results printed outside tcl to stdout/stderr.
           fflush
           switch $error_code {
-- 
